  "question": {
    "text": "The parameter that remains the same for molecules of all gases at a given temperature is :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "kinetic energy",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "momentum",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "mass",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "speed",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>From the kinetic interpretation of temperature, we know, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mi>T</mi></math>. Clearly, it depends only on temperature.</p>"
  }
